# Runtime secrets, as 1Password references resolved by `op run` at boot.
# This file holds NO secret values — only op://<vault>/<item>/<field> pointers.
# Ruddick owns the vault; the service's only sealed Railway variable is
# OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN, which lets `op run` read these items. Items are
# Password items named after the env var, field `password`.
#
# Bucket credentials are NOT here: Railway buckets are attached to the service
# as reference variables (Bucket → Credentials → Add to service), so Litestream
# and the corpus reader get theirs from Railway directly.
#
# `op run` fails at boot if a referenced item does not exist, so only list
# items that are in the vault; add a provider's key line when its item exists.
SESSION_SECRET=op://spiritolo-staging/SESSION_SECRET/password
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=op://spiritolo-staging/DEEPSEEK_API_KEY/password
TAILSCALE_AUTHKEY=op://spiritolo-staging/TAILSCALE_AUTHKEY/password
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=op://spiritolo-staging/ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/password
# OPENAI_API_KEY=op://spiritolo-staging/OPENAI_API_KEY/password
